Three inbound webhook/secret checks compare with a plain `!==`, which is not constant-time (CWE-208). The repo already uses the correct pattern (`crypto.timingSafeEqual`) in the BTCPay handler and in OAuth state decoding, so this is a consistency fix.

**Locations (at commit `abffde3`):**

- `packages/app-store/hitpay/api/webhook.ts` (HMAC vs payload field)

```ts
if (signed !== obj.hmac) {
  throw new HttpCode({ statusCode: 400, message: "Bad Request" });
}
```

- `packages/features/calendar-subscription/adapters/GoogleCalendarSubscription.adapter.ts`

```ts
if (token !== this.GOOGLE_WEBHOOK_TOKEN) {
  log.warn("Invalid webhook token");
  return false;
}
```

- `apps/web/app/api/webhook/app-credential/route.ts` (only when credential sharing is enabled)

```ts
if (secretHeader !== CREDENTIAL_SYNC_SECRET) {
  return NextResponse.json({ message: "Invalid credential sync secret" }, { status: 403 });
}
```

**Reference pattern already in the repo** — `packages/app-store/btcpayserver/api/webhook.ts`:

```ts
if (computedSignature.length !== expectedSignature.length) {
  throw new HttpCode({ statusCode: 400, message: "signature mismatch" });
}
const isValid = crypto.timingSafeEqual(
  Buffer.from(computedSignature, "hex"),
  Buffer.from(expectedSignature, "hex")
);
```

**Suggested change:** length pre-check + `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length buffers, same as BTCPay.

**Severity:** low. Timing attacks against HMAC/secret comparison over the network are hard in practice because of jitter. Defense-in-depth / consistency, not a reported vulnerability. No proof-of-concept.

Static review of public source only; no traffic sent to any Cal.com environment.

